Event record copy boundary
==========================

Run from any working directory:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/sparklink/run_event_copy.py

The runner compiles the complete current sle_event.rs unchanged and the actual
SparkLinkCtl::read_iter method. Kernel errno, mutex, iterator and unused in-place
initializer dependencies have explicit fixtures. Nine tests cover all partial
copy positions of the first/later record, zero/short buffers, capacity tails,
bounded ring wrap/overflow, actual BroadcastRing fan-out and serialized shared-fd
commit. Successful earlier records may be returned; an incomplete final record
is retained and excluded from the returned count. No new production test hook.

This is actual function coverage with dependency fixtures, not a live read(2)
page fault, kernel mutex/lockdep, controller routing, removal wakeup or RF proof.
The old DLI_POLL_EVENT ring/backend consumption is a different legacy path and
still awaits migration to the independent controller event subscription.
